# XCU cflow
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# cflow run on small C sources whose line numbers are known; the exact type
# text, order of callees and spacing are not specified, so the checks read
# the reference number, the indentation column of each name, the angle-
# bracket location and the presence of names.

assertion  XCU.cflow.001
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Each output line starts with its line number as the reference
           number, callees are indented deeper than their callers, a
           definition from C source ends with the file name and line number
           in angle brackets, and by default only functions not starting
           with an underscore are shown.
note       Q-178 in docs/standard-issues.md: the format string and the
           example leave the indentation and repeated calls open; the test
           reads indentation as the name column and checks a repeat only
           under a different caller.
test       t/001-graph-format.sh

assertion  XCU.cflow.002
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Once a name has been written with its definition, a later mention
           of it carries the reference number of that line and no
           definition.
note       Q-178 in docs/standard-issues.md: the format string and the
           example leave the indentation and repeated calls open; the test
           reads indentation as the name column and checks a repeat only
           under a different caller.
test       t/002-repeated-callee.sh

assertion  XCU.cflow.003
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With -r the listing shows the callers of each function, indented
           under the callee, and the callees at the outermost level are in
           lexicographic order.
test       t/003-reverse.sh

assertion  XCU.cflow.004
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -d with a small depth cuts deeper callees from the graph, a large
           depth changes nothing, and a depth of zero or a negative number
           is ignored.
test       t/004-depth.sh

assertion  XCU.cflow.005
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -i x adds external and static data symbols to the graph, -i _
           adds names that begin with an underscore, and each is absent
           without its option.
test       t/005-include-symbols.sh

assertion  XCU.cflow.006
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -D defines a macro, -U removes it, the later of -D and -U for a
           name wins, and -I adds a directory searched for quoted include
           files.
note       Q-177 in docs/standard-issues.md: the synopsis says -U dir; the
           test gives -U a macro name as c17 does.
test       t/006-preprocessor-options.sh

assertion  XCU.cflow.007
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A file operand that cannot be read gives a non-zero exit status.
test       t/007-missing-file.sh

assertion  XCU.cflow.008
anchor     utilities/cflow.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A file with the suffix .i is taken as the output of preprocessing
           C source and gives the same call graph.
test       t/008-preprocessed-input.sh
